# Source-distribution contents beyond what setuptools-scm's file finder provides.
#
# Why this file is necessary:
#
# The RPM spec's %install reads these paths directly out of the unpacked sdist:
#
#     packaging/systemd/powerpack-mcp.service
#     packaging/nginx/powerpack-mcp.fragment
#     packaging/nginx/powerpack-mcp-zone.conf
#     docs/operations.md
#
# setuptools-scm populates the sdist from git-tracked files, so files that are not yet
# committed are silently omitted, and `rpmbuild` then fails at %install.  The RPM is built
# from an sdist, so an sdist missing these files cannot produce a package at all.
#
# `graft` matches on the filesystem, not on git, so the sdist is correct whether or not
# the files happen to be committed.  `.github/workflows/packaging.yml` also asserts the
# sdist contains these paths, so a missing file fails at sdist build time.
graft packaging
graft docs
include LICENSE

# Deliberately not pruned: Dockerfile, docker-compose*.yml, .github/ and tests/ remain in
# the sdist.  This is not the enforcement point: they are excluded from the RPM payload,
# which %files achieves by listing only what is wanted.  Pruning them here would create a
# second, weaker place to get that wrong.
